## Steps to reproduce

1. Bring up the target container from the `Prerequisites` section.
2. Save the test file as `poc.mjs`.
3. Run the script.

```
node poc.mjs
```

Exit status 0 means reproduced.

Every case is the same harness, the same browser, the same profile, and the same single navigation. The only thing that changes is the state of the application being authorized. Cases 1 and 4 are the discriminators: case 1 confirms the same page is capable of stopping and asking; case 4 confirms the same page is capable of halting on the OIDC path when re-authentication is required. A harness that simply granted everything would have failed both.

Reproduced requires all of: case 1 issues no token after the page load; the deliberate approval produces a consent record and an approved code does exchange; case 2 issues a token after one page load and that token's subject equals the victim's identifier; case 3 issues a token with no pre-existing consent record; and case 4 issues no token. Any of those failing reports not-reproduced. In particular, a run that granted in case 1 or case 4 would be reporting a broken harness, not a finding.

